@startuml

title 03. Customers and suppliers

hide circle
skinparam linetype ortho

entity Customer {
	* id: int
	--
	* name: string(255)
	phone: string(255)?
	email: string(255)?
	comment: text?
	* status: ActiveStatusEnum
	* createdAt: DateTimeImmutable
	* updatedAt: DateTimeImmutable
	deletedAt: DateTimeImmutable?
	* store: Store
	createdBy: User?
	updatedBy: User?
}

entity Supplier {
	* id: int
	--
	* name: string(255)
	phone: string(255)?
	email: string(255)?
	comment: text?
	* status: ActiveStatusEnum
	* createdAt: DateTimeImmutable
	* updatedAt: DateTimeImmutable
	deletedAt: DateTimeImmutable?
	* store: Store
	createdBy: User?
	updatedBy: User?
}

Store ||--o{ Customer : has customers
Store ||--o{ Supplier : has suppliers
Customer |o--o{ Order : places
Supplier |o--o{ Purchase : supplies
User |o--o{ Customer : creates/updates
User |o--o{ Supplier : creates/updates

note right of Customer
  Current project status:
  - Customer entity is not implemented.
  - Customer CRUD is not implemented.
  - Order currently stores customer snapshot fields,
    but has no Customer relation yet.

  Required behavior:
  - Customer belongs to one Store.
  - Deletion should be soft delete through deletedAt.
  - Customer can be inactive without deleting historical orders.
  - Order must copy customer name/phone/email to snapshots.
end note

note right of Supplier
  Current project status:
  - Supplier entity is not implemented.
  - Supplier CRUD is not implemented.
  - Purchase currently stores supplier snapshot fields,
    but has no Supplier relation yet.

  Required behavior:
  - Supplier belongs to one Store.
  - Purchase must copy supplier name/phone/email to snapshots.
  - Historical purchases must remain readable
    even when supplier is edited or soft deleted.
end note

note bottom
  Suggested implementation steps:

  1. Add Customer and Supplier entities/repositories/managers.
  2. Add unique suggestions if needed:
     (store_id, email) where email is not null,
     (store_id, phone) where phone is not null.
  3. Add admin CRUD and filters for both.
  4. Add fixtures with a few customers and suppliers.
  5. Update Order/Purchase forms later to select customer/supplier.
  6. Add tests for store scoping and snapshot copying.

  Do this before Sales Orders and Purchases.
end note

@enduml
